# Thunder Fighter Refactor Rules

## Current Stage

The current stage is behavior-preserving refactoring only.

Do not introduce SDL, WebAssembly, mobile support, new gameplay logic, new rendering logic, or new input logic in this stage.

## Hard Rules

1. Do not rewrite the whole project at once.
2. Keep every step buildable.
3. Do not change gameplay behavior unless explicitly requested.
4. Do not change enemy spawning logic.
5. Do not change bullet logic.
6. Do not change collision logic.
7. Do not change score logic.
8. Do not change leaderboard logic.
9. Do not change menu flow.
10. Do not change keyboard bindings.
11. Do not change visual output.
12. Do not introduce SDL in the current stage.
13. Do not introduce WebAssembly in the current stage.
14. Do not introduce mobile-specific code in the current stage.

## Allowed Refactoring

The following changes are allowed only when explicitly requested:

1. Split large files.
2. Move existing types into separate headers.
3. Move existing constants into config headers.
4. Move existing console input code into separate files.
5. Move existing console rendering code into separate files.
6. Move existing high score file I/O into separate files.
7. Reorder class methods for readability.
8. Rename functions only when behavior remains identical.
9. Update CMake only to include newly split files.

## Forbidden Refactoring

1. Do not redesign the whole architecture in one step.
2. Do not create a new GameCore yet unless explicitly requested.
3. Do not create SDL frontend yet.
4. Do not delete the old terminal version.
5. Do not replace FTXUI yet.
6. Do not optimize gameplay values.
7. Do not rebalance difficulty.
8. Do not change file formats.

## Build Rule

After every code modification, run the existing CMake configure and build commands.

If the build fails, stop and report the exact error before continuing.

## Long-Term Direction

The long-term goal is:

1. Behavior-preserving cleanup.
2. Separate platform-specific code.
3. Extract platform-independent game logic.
4. Add SDL desktop frontend.
5. Prepare WebAssembly support.
6. Prepare mobile support.

But the current stage is only step 1.
